The graph shows a population modelled by $P=\dfrac{C}{1+Ae^{-kt}}$, with $t$ in years. Write down the carrying capacity and the initial population from the graph, then find $A$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$t$}, ylabel={$P$}, xmin=-1, xmax=15, ymin=-60, ymax=700, xtick={5,10}, ytick={100,600}, samples=120, clip=false, ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick, ->, domain=0:14] {600/(1+5*exp(-0.5*x))};
\addplot[dashed, domain=0:15] (x, 600);
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
